ADR-0049 §"Open work" step 3 -- adjudicated findings per shape -- is the last
gate before the deferred-crossing family may be retagged, and it is the one
that asks what the family's findings are actually WORTH. Two arms, and they
disagree, and the disagreement is the result.

ARM 1, from measurement 0006's own two-pass labels: the family is 7 situations
of 112 (11 rows), 0 TP, 0 useful, against a 33.0% population. ARM 2, a fresh
census over 0006's sixteen repositories plus caddy: 50 situations / 411 rows,
48.0% correctness, 22.0% useful.

SHAPE IS NOT THE DISCRIMINATOR. What the source line does is:

  DEFERRED       arrival really is in another scope        3    0 TP   0 useful
  WIRING         cmd.Stdin = os.Stdin, never read here     8    0 TP   0 useful
  WRONG-CHANNEL  wraps a file or a buffer, not stdin      17   10 TP   0 useful
  READ-IN-SCOPE  the handle is read where it was built    22   14 TP  11 useful

THE REFUTATION CONDITION WAS WRITTEN DOWN BEFORE ANY LABEL AND IT FIRED,
ELEVEN TIMES. bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin) returns a handle and so fails ruling 1
exactly as ListenAndServe does -- but it is read four lines later in the same
function, so "the scope the call does not name" IS the caller's and the mint is
not a mis-attribution. Go's ENTIRE stdin surface is three deferred-crossing
rows and the catalogue has no ReadString/Scan/Text/File.Read to relocate a
crossing to, so retagging the HANDLE shape is forbidden by ruling 3 on its own
terms. Catalogue the reads first.

LAUNCH IS UNANIMOUS AND THIN, and the second half is published as loudly as the
first: every adjudicated launch-family finding in both arms is a false positive
(2 here, 4 in 0006), and that is ALL the evidence 17 repositories contain. An
over-counting grep finds 49 files with a launch-shaped call against 2 findings,
because jaeger returned inconclusive on all three untrusted-input claims and
cilium's framework rows are WI-lalot-inert. The retag is a correctness fix
worth about two findings, not a precision fix.

REGISTER, LAZY and CALLBACK produced no findings at all. That is absence of
evidence, not evidence of harmlessness, and step 3 is not cleared for them.

FIRST CONFIGURED-ACTION FINDINGS THIS PROJECT HAS ADJUDICATED -- three, all in
caddy, including ADR-0046's own motivating example citable clause by clause.
0006 reported zero structurally; ADR-0046 said a cohort meant to exercise the
class must contain one, so this one does.

TWO REGISTER CORRECTIONS AND AN ARTIFACT TRAP. ets:foldl is a TRANSFER, not
callback-delivered -- it returns the accumulator, unlike ftplib.retrbinary
which returns a status; 15 situations, 23% of the raw join, moved out of the
family on that. And measurement_0006/ledger-final.json IS NOT FINAL: it carries
the blind pass's 44 TPs while the published 38 is what survives pass 4's
refutations, which live in a separate file. Arm 1 asserted 38 against the file
whose name says "final", failed, and only then found them -- tmux#3 is one of
the seven refuted, so it is an FP here and would have been published as a TP.
Filed as WI-tuhop.

TWO CLAIMS IN STEP 3 ITSELF WERE WRONG AND ARE CORRECTED IN PLACE. 0006's
corpus does not contain caddy (it was 0005's, and 0006 excluded 0005's five by
construction -- which is exactly why 0006 could call its zero CONFIGURED-ACTION
count structural rather than lucky). And it is not true that zero launch-family
findings appear among the 112: seven do, three of them the C socket datapoint
the same sentence went on to name. The ADR's "Implementation state" claim that
no catalogue row uses net_listen is excised too; eleven have since INV-kanuk.

